{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"[operator-attested] Full-suite evidence for the final AC. Both runs are the CI-gating selection (`make test` = `pytest -m 'not integration and not external' -q`) in the worktree ../c6c9-attest-split.\n\nPRE-SPLIT (tree at origin/main c3fb869ab5, before any edit):\n    1 failed, 10214 passed, 38 skipped, 222 deselected, 18 warnings, 3 errors in 2160.80s (0:36:00)\n\nPOST-SPLIT (commit 5e08c9053db):\n    1 failed, 10214 passed, 38 skipped, 222 deselected, 18 warnings in 2119.19s (0:35:19)\n\nTest count is IDENTICAL (10214 passed / 38 skipped / 222 deselected both sides). No new seam tests were added: the move is behavior-preserving and the existing remediation-gate suite already exercises the seam (proof below), so a new test would only have been a change-detector.\n\nThe 1 failure is the SAME test on both sides — tests/unit/test_identity_gate_scope_and_ledger.py::test_ledger_non_null_commit_sha_reresolves_after_history_rewrite — an identity/ledger test with no relation to plan_review. Independently confirmed pre-existing by checking out origin/main content and running it alone: still fails (AssertionError at test_identity_gate_scope_and_ledger.py:307).\n\nThe 3 errors in the PRE-split run were 'Test leaked new entries into REPO_ROOT' and were caused by MY OWN concurrent rebar writes (edit/claim/comment/session-log) into the worktree store while that run was in flight. They are absent from the post-split run, which I ran with no concurrent rebar commands. Not attributable to the refactor.\n\nMUTATION / TEETH CHECK (the reason I am confident this is not a silent-breakage refactor): the moved code resolves current_material_fingerprint and registry_version through FUNCTION-LOCAL 'from .attest import ...' so the attribute is re-read per call. I verified this is load-bearing rather than defensive by applying the naive alternative — hoisting those imports to module level — and re-running: 4 tests in tests/unit/test_plan_review_remediation_gate.py go RED (test_all_preconditions_met_is_eligible, test_no_signature_with_sidecar_baseline_is_eligible, test_signature_branch_unchanged_and_tagged, test_window_reset_on_each_review_keeps_loop_alive). Reverted; green again.\n\nPURE-MOVE PROOF: diff of the extracted cluster against the original attest.py lines 241-382 is empty apart from the two added function-local import statements. Every executable line is byte-identical.\n\nFinal sizes: attest.py 794 -> 656 (AC1: under 700); remediation_mode.py 182 (AC2: at least 100); zero test edits required (AC3).\n\nGates: make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS (mypy, 433 source files)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785896687825437001,"uuid":"411c7380-4f2a-4203-b1ca-8772ae4296b0"}